\item \textbf{Causal mechanism and data contamination.} The study establishes correlational evidence with controlled stratification; mechanistic analysis at the attention or logit level is needed to confirm the causal pathway. A post-hoc renaming experiment (Appendix~\ref{app:renaming}) suggests SCS may proxy deeper conceptual overlap rather than surface similarity. FewRel (2018) may appear in pretraining corpora, but train-origin relations show lower accuracy than val-origin, opposite to the contamination hypothesis; DocRED (2019) provides a lower-contamination-risk replication (Appendix~\ref{app:split-origin}).
